  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Best Buy - HomeConnections",
    "description": "Worked with a large agile team to develop a web based in-store and call center application for comparison shopping and selling home connectivity services. Our team maintained a suite of over 3000 PHP Unit tests, developed a REST Level 3 API that can be consumed in JSON. We also maintained a suite of XML SOAP service stubs and scenarios for quick replay, quality control, and application testing.\n\nMy role consisted of working closely with other team members, determining development tasks to meet business requirements, code review, very thorough API documentation, developing and maintaining new areas of the hypermedia platform, developing and maintaining hypermedia schema, and aiding lead developers during application deployments. We also maintained a suite of API level tests which could identify when new requirements affected our platform's workflows.\n\nThis was one of the coolest platforms I've ever had the opportunity to develop.\n\nTechnologies most applied:\n- Symfony 2 (PHP5.4)\n- PHPUnit\n- REST (Level 3), http://martinfowler.com/articles/richardsonMaturityModel.html\n- XML, SOAP\n- JSON, YAML, Markdown (document formats)\n\nNew technologies applied:\n- Node.js (server side javascript)\n- Angular (javascript)\n- Twig (for Symfony 2)\n- bash",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2013 - Feb 2014"
   }
